[x] Protect the known critical semantics =protect-critical-semantics $DONE 2026-08-14. Action, reference-routing, template-targeting, and high-risk durable Action/Charter/Plan lifecycle semantics now have focused executable protection. Template targeting uses declared identity/parent scenarios and retained a 5 caught / 0 missed module result. Durable Action/Charter mutation analysis moved from 20 missed to three explicit OS-boundary residuals; targeted Plan lifecycle moved from 13 missed to none. Exact tests exposed and fixed unsafe post-lock name/alias fallback, mutating charter dry-runs, parent-directory source-path traversal, cross-Plan token confusion, unrelated-action token confusion, and incomplete VTODO import/tally assertions. Production simplifications removed redundant existence and Plan eligibility checks. Residuals are directory fsync observability, equivalent explicit unlock-on-drop, and non-portable injection of non-contention OS lock failure.$ !1 %2026-08-14T15:47 #019ffc5b-d063-76e0-be9d-93f1b50e2954
[x] Retain only demonstrated test support =demonstrated-test-support $DONE 2026-08-14. Reviewed the assurance support against its actual consumers. Kept the Action, reference, and template generators repository-local; each declares its own semantic oracle and directly serves the properties that need it. Kept the pre-existing exact template units because they produced the already-discriminating baseline and localize simple failures, while the generator covers distinct mixed hierarchy/field/source states. Kept parser conformance fixtures only for byte-level escaping and recovery contracts. Durable lifecycle protection uses direct state-transition and crash-point tests, with no generalized fixture or shared generator framework added.$ !2 %2026-08-14T15:47 <protect-critical-semantics #019ffc5b-d06f-7d33-9d88-fa2890c59cf3
[x] Validate the pinned platform composition =validate-pinned-platform $DONE 2026-08-14. Added scripts/validate-pinned and documented it in the platform README. The command first rejects uninitialized, conflicted, or gitlink-mismatched submodules, then directly invokes the existing pre-push gates owned by tree-sitter-actions, Core, CLI, graphd, LSP, Neovim, and ontology; specifications is explicitly reported as having no executable repository gate. The command passed end to end against the exact eight staged submodule revisions. No generalized validation framework, depth taxonomy, or duplicate repository checks were introduced.$ !2 %2026-08-14T15:58 <protect-critical-semantics #019ffc5b-d07b-7653-b695-843c0e41a530
[x] Record lessons and close executable assurance =close-executable-assurance $DONE 2026-08-14. Recorded the focused generator, mutation, and pinned-platform commands; technique lessons; rationales for the three durability residuals; and concrete promotion triggers for future bounded assurance work. Reviewed the done gate: reference, template, and lifecycle seams are protected or explicitly dispositioned; retained support has demonstrated value; reproducible commands are recorded; scripts/validate-pinned passed the exact platform composition; and remaining risks/triggers are documented. This bounded assurance uplift is ready to close.$ !3 %2026-08-14T15:59 <demonstrated-test-support <validate-pinned-platform #019ffc5b-d087-7d00-957d-46c4f82eb6cd
